    "datePosted": "2026-11-24T13:23:27.000Z",
    "description": "The Skilled Workforce for Innovation and Financial Sector Transformation (SWIFT) Program, implemented by BKP Economic Advisors in partnership with the National Bank of Ethiopia (NBE) and the Mastercard Foundation, invites qualified firms to submit proposals to design, develop, pilot, and support the national rollout of the Ethiopian Academy of Finance (EAF)'s Career Orientation Initiative (COI). The selected firm will help turn the COI concept into a high-quality, scalable, and sustainable initiative that prepares young people for careers in Ethiopia's financial sector. The assignment includes curriculum and learning design, career services, employer engagement, trainer development, pilot implementation, and national rollout support. A key objective is to strengthen EAF's capacity to manage, deliver, and continuously improve the initiative beyond the life of the assignment. Overall Objective : To support EAF in establishing a nationally coordinated, inclusive and sustainable COI that responds to participant and labour-market needs, strengthens young people’s career awareness, readiness and employability, connects them with financial-sector opportunities, and creates pathways to EAF learning, internships, employment and lifelong professional development, supported by the institutional capacity and partnerships needed for sustainable scale-up. Specific Objectives : The COI will pursue four integrated objectives: Establish an evidence-based and market-responsive foundation through a rapid Training Needs Assessment (TNA), labour-market and stakeholder assessment to identify participant needs, employer expectations, career information gaps and delivery requirements, while supporting NBE/EAF alignment with relevant financial learning and literacy initiatives and identifying practical policy and institutional measures to strengthen the learning-to-work pathway. Design and operationalize a coherent, competency-based learning and delivery system through a modular curriculum, clear learning pathways, standardized trainer and participant materials, digital/blended resources and assessment tools contextualized to Ethiopia, supported by approximately 30 certified trainers/facilitators and early-delivery coaching and backstopping. Establish effective career services, industry linkages and progression mechanisms through career profiling, coaching, mentoring, employer engagement, internships and referrals; development of scalable career-services and employer-engagement arrangements; and design of the EAF Graduate/Talent Database specifications and interim participant-tracking arrangements for subsequent integration with EAF/SWIFT digital systems, subject to approval, consent and data-protection requirements. Institutionalize a sustainable and quality-assured COI within EAF by embedding QA, MEL, research, knowledge management, risk management and continuous improvement, while strengthening EAF capacity and ownership and integrating COI into its regular portfolio and wider learning ecosystem.",
