    "description": "LonAdd HR Consultancy Plc (www.lonadd.com) is a Recruitment & Outsourcing Company based in Addis Abeba, Ethiopia, with branch offices in Dukem, Hawassa and Bahir Dar. We are looking to recruit Factory Finance Manager to join On Behalf of Our Client. Job Location : Oromia Region Number required:- 1 (One) Position Purpose The Factory Finance Manager is responsible for overseeing all factory finance activities, including product costing, inventory accounting, manufacturing performance analysis, invoicing control, revenue assurance, budgeting support, and operational financial controls. The role acts as the key business partner to production, supply chain, logistics, and commercial teams to ensure accurate financial reporting, strong controls, cost efficiency, and revenue integrity across the brewery operation. The role also owns the end-to-end control process from production through dispatch, invoicing, and revenue recognition. Key Accountabilities Product Costing and Cost Management Key Responsibilities Develop and maintain standard costs for all finished goods and packaging materials. Review and validate Bills of Materials (BOMs) and production recipes. Analyze production cost variances, including: Raw material variances Labor variances Manufacturing overhead variances Yield variances Monitor conversion costs and cost per hectoliter (HL). Support product profitability and margin analysis. Review cost impacts arising from production inefficiencies and process losses. Recommend cost optimization initiatives to factory management. Inventory Management and Control Key Responsibilities Ensure accurate valuation of raw materials, packaging materials, work-in-progress, and finished goods inventory. Review daily, weekly, and monthly inventory reconciliations. Monitor inventory movement and aging. Review stock adjustments and inventory write-offs. Participate in periodic physical inventory counts. Ensure compliance with inventory management policies. Investigate and report inventory gains and losses. Manufacturing Performance Analysis Key Responsibilities Analyze operational and financial performance indicators. Track factory KPIs, including: Production volume Yield percentage Material utilization Utility consumption Machine efficiency Waste percentages Conversion cost per HL Evaluate production efficiency trends. Provide financial insights supporting operational improvement initiatives. Present monthly performance reviews to management. Invoicing Control and Revenue Assurance Key Responsibilities Invoice Governance Ensure all dispatches are supported by approved and valid invoices. Review daily dispatch-to-invoice reconciliation reports. Verify completeness and accuracy of invoices generated through the ERP system. Ensure all invoices comply with approved customer pricing agreements. Ensure invoice numbering sequence complies with legal and company requirements. Monitor invoice cancellation and amendment controls. Revenue Assurance Ensure all delivered products are invoiced on a timely basis. Monitor and investigate unbilled deliveries. Review daily sales, dispatch, and invoicing reconciliations. Ensure complete and accurate revenue recognition. Identify and investigate revenue leakage risks. Pricing and Commercial Controls Review pricing accuracy and price master updates. Validate discounts, promotions, rebates, and trade schemes. Monitor price override transactions. Ensure commercial approvals are properly documented. Tax Compliance Ensure VAT and other applicable taxes are accurately calculated. Verify tax invoice compliance with regulatory requirements. Coordinate with tax and accounting teams for tax reporting accuracy. Customer Billing Support Resolve invoice disputes in collaboration with Sales and Distribution teams. Review customer claims related to billing discrepancies. Support collection activities by ensuring invoice accuracy and completeness. Financial Planning and Budgeting Support Key Responsibilities Support annual budgeting and periodic forecasting processes. Prepare manufacturing cost forecasts. Provide operational assumptions for financial planning. Support CAPEX and investment evaluations. Analyze budget variances and recommend corrective actions. Internal Controls and Compliance Key Responsibilities Ensure compliance with company financial policies and SOPs. Maintain adequate segregation of duties over: Production Dispatch Invoicing Collections Inventory management Review and strengthen factory financial controls. Support internal and external audits. Ensure timely closure of audit observations. Promote a strong control and compliance culture across operations. Financial Reporting Key Responsibilities Prepare monthly factory performance reports. Support month-end and year-end closing activities. Review inventory-related journal entries. Reconcile manufacturing and inventory accounts. Support preparation of management reports and Board submissions.",
