    "datePosted": "2026-11-24T08:20:48.000Z",
    "description": "Medical Teams Calling Daring to love like Jesus, we boldly break barriers to health and restore wholeness in a hurting world. Medical Teams International holds strict child and vulnerable adult safeguarding principles and a zero-tolerance policy for misconduct related to sexual harassment, exploitation and abuse in the workplace and other places where the organization’s activities are rendered. Parallel to technical competence, recruitment & selection, hiring decisions will give due emphasis to assessing candidates' eligibility thorough background checks, police clearance, and professional reference check processes. JOB SUMMARY The Food Security Specialist / General Food Distribution (GFD) and School Feeding (SF) Specialist is a senior position based at the MTI Ethiopia Country Office in Addis Ababa, working under the technical direction and support of the Nutrition Advisor. The position provides strategic leadership, technical oversight, and operational support for General Food Distribution, School Feeding, food security, and resilience-building programmes implemented in partnership with the World Food Programme (WFP) across refugee camps and host communities in Ethiopia. The Specialist is responsible for strengthening programme quality throughout the project cycle, ensuring the effective management and accountable distribution of food and nutrition commodities, supporting emergency response and recovery interventions, and promoting sustainable food security and livelihood resilience outcomes for vulnerable populations. The role also includes capacity building of field teams, monitoring programme performance, consolidating high-quality reports, conducting regular field support missions, and representing MTI in coordination forums with government authorities, UN agencies, and other partners. The position requires extensive experience in food security, humanitarian assistance, resilience programming, and multi-sectoral coordination, as well as strong skills in leadership, partnership management, planning, monitoring, communication, and team development. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Provide strategic leadership and technical oversight for MTI/WFP General Food Distribution (GFD) and School Feeding (SF) programmes across all operational locations. Support the design, planning, budgeting, and implementation of GFD and SF projects in line with donor requirements and approved agreements. Ensure GFD and SF activities are implemented in compliance with FLAs, SOPs, programme guidelines, and organizational policies. Coordinate food commodity requests, pipeline planning, and distribution schedules with field teams and WFP. Oversee commodity management processes, including receipt, storage, transportation, tracking, distribution, and reporting. Support beneficiary registration, verification, and distribution processes in coordination with relevant stakeholders. Monitor programme implementation to ensure accountability, quality, efficiency, and compliance with humanitarian standards. Conduct regular field visits to distribution sites, warehouses, and schools to provide technical support, identify gaps, and improve programme performance. Provide technical guidance, coaching, mentoring, and capacity building to GFD and SF staff. Ensure the integration of protection, gender, disability inclusion, safeguarding, and accountability principles across programme implementation. Strengthen coordination between GFD, School Feeding, nutrition, and food security interventions to improve beneficiary outcomes. Review and consolidate programme reports, ensuring accuracy, completeness, and timely submission to MTI and WFP. Collaborate with the MEAL team to strengthen monitoring systems, track indicators, and support programme evaluations and post-distribution monitoring. Analyze programme data and monitoring findings to support informed decision-making and continuous improvement. Prepare field monitoring reports and follow up on agreed action points. Represent MTI in national and field-level coordination meetings, technical working groups, and partner engagements related to food assistance and school feeding. Maintain effective working relationships with WFP, UNHCR, RRS, government counterparts, and other stakeholders. Support recruitment, performance management, and professional development of GFD and SF staff. Monitor programme budgets, spending plans, commodity pipelines, and resource utilization in coordination with Finance and Logistics teams. Ensure compliance with MTI policies, including Code of Conduct, PSEA, Child Safeguarding, Safety and Security, and donor requirements. Support emergency food assistance responses and contingency planning as required. Reporting: Ensure timely preparation and submission of GFD and School Feeding reports, commodity reports, and programme updates. Review, consolidate, and validate field reports before submission to MTI and WFP. Support field teams in maintaining accurate beneficiary, commodity, and distribution records. Coordinate monitoring, post-distribution monitoring, and programme review activities with the MEAL team. Document and share key findings, lessons learned, best practices, and recommendations for programme improvement.",
