    "description": "Medical Teams Calling Daring to love like Jesus, we boldly break barriers to health and restore wholeness in a hurting world. Medical Teams International holds strict child and vulnerable adult safeguarding principles and a zero-tolerance policy for misconduct related to sexual harassment, exploitation and abuse in the workplace and other places where the organization’s activities are rendered. Parallel to technical competence, recruitment & selection, hiring decisions will give due emphasis to assessing candidates' eligibility thorough background checks, police clearance, and professional reference check processes. JOB SUMMARY The GDT Controller/SF Supervisor is responsible to carry out day-to-day General Food Distribution and school feeding activities under the supervision of the GFD/SF Officer. GDT Controller/SF supervisor will be responsible for the Verification of beneficiaries' identity, issuing the food ration to the beneficiaries, reporting daily release and controlling the crowd and queue management. In addition, S/he will be tasked with facilitating, monitoring, supervising, and coordinating smooth school feeding operations which include stock management and Hygiene and sanitation management. The post holder will also be responsible for ensuring proper Reporting, and coordination, Monitoring supervision with various departments including education, child protection programs and other support units. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES General food Distribution (GFD) Verify Beneficiaries’ identity and take their thumbprint in the distribution site as per supervisor guidance. Communicate with beneficiaries with respect and assist vulnerable beneficiaries are given needed considerations Issue food basket release orders to the intended beneficiaries. Monitor the daily flow of food commodities to beneficiaries. reporting daily release and controlling the crowd and queue management Ensure that all equipment, food, and supplies are available for the assigned period/daily operation/s on the FDP Warehouse. Review, prepare, and submit daily reports of delivered and distributed food. Manage crowd and ensure proper alignment of beneficiaries, especially women and those of special needs in front of FDPs. Do any related task asked by the supervisor. By using General food distribution tool (GDT), the GDT controller/distributor will plan the allocated food (identification of the type and quantity of assistance) , determine the distribution plan. Communicate and conduct pre distribution meeting. Disseminate of assistance related information through community-based structure and other mechanisms. Among others it includes the type and quantity of assistance and time/date of distribution as well as any delays of supplies. Identify eligible family /individuals during assistance distribution exercise. during this time, the admitter is stationed at the main entrance of the distribution facility Verify the identity of the eligible representatives of a household or the approved alternate assistance collector Distribute the food to legitimate beneficiaries Ensure the beneficiaries has collected all the entitled commodities Overseeing that each ration is complete and is organized in an orderly stack at the distribution Identifying vulnerable beneficiaries (widows, pregnant women, elderly) to ensure they have priority in receiving their rations Mobilize and raise awareness about the organization, program objectives and activities to local authorities and the population, and act as a link between the organization and the beneficiaries at the program site Support the integration of accountability practices into program activities by following established procedures during planning, implementation, monitoring, and reporting. Help ensure that accountability is reflected in day-to-day tasks, team interactions, and when working with partners or communities. Support safeguarding of program participants and employees through promoting an environment of awareness and upholding the code of conduct provisions of Medical Teams Protection from Sexual Exploitation & Abuse, Child & Vulnerable Adult protection, and harassment-free workplace policies. Incumbents will remain alert and responsive to any child and adult safeguarding risks, acquire relevant knowledge and skills which will enable you to promote strong safeguarding practices, understand the child and adult safeguarding policy and procedures, and conduct yourself in a manner consistent with the Safeguarding code of conduct and behavior expectations. School Feeding Program (SFP) Daily, weekly and monthly Reporting of SFP. Day to day management of stock movements. Monitoring, supervising and ensure SFP SOP guideline are used accordingly for CSB+ when cooking and serving for the student. Supervising Monitoring of kitchen, cooks, dinner hall, toilets, garbage pitch hygiene and sanitation situation better health. Timely reporting any gaps, including stock out of commodities before one week ahead. Regular updating of day-to-day situations of the feeding. Monitoring whether the kitchen is clean and the floors dry at all time Daily supervision on the cooks cover hair? Keep the nails short and use overcoat or special cloths every time they are at the kitchen or preparing porridge. Ensure hand washing at the kitchen, dining room, and toilets full of water, with soap Monitor cooker to meet the standard of hygiene when mixing the preparing porridge? Ensure the cookers use the standard guide line when cooking the porridge (use look up table) supervising cooker and cleaner how they are using the soap when washing the materials Ensure all cooks have medical evaluation/certificate for every 6 months? Ensure to dispose all waste food and garbage in Appropriately Place. Perform weekly checks on the store balance using sock out stock in movements document way-bill and hand overing note for any difference report to school feeding officer Ensure effective management of the cooks, cleaners and wood cutters making sure that their weekly tasks are achieved. Conduct regular meetings with all the subordinate staff’s cooks, and cleaners in order to contribute high standard for hygiene and sanitation",
