    "description": "Medical Teams Calling Daring to love like Jesus, we boldly break barriers to health and restore wholeness in a hurting world. Medical Teams International holds strict child and vulnerable adult safeguarding principles and a zero-tolerance policy for misconduct related to sexual harassment, exploitation and abuse in the workplace and other places where the organization’s activities are rendered. Parallel to technical competence, recruitment & selection, hiring decisions will give due emphasis to assessing candidates' eligibility thorough background checks, police clearance, and professional reference check processes. JOB SUMMARY The Biometric Supervisor is responsible for accurately registering and verifying beneficiary information in line with UNHCR registration criteria; overseeing the safety of the entire distribution site; ensuring that each family receives its full food entitlement; and accurately reporting the number of rations distributed. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Liaise with the GFD/SF senior officer, partners, community leaders, and other stakeholders to ensure smooth food distribution to beneficiaries. Use the General Food Distribution Tool (GDT) to plan the allocated food, including the type and quantity of assistance, and to determine the distribution plan. Identify eligible families and individuals during the assistance distribution exercise, stationed at the main entrance of the distribution facility. Verify the identity of the eligible household representative or the approved alternate assistance collector. Distribute food to legitimate beneficiaries. Ensure beneficiaries collect all of their entitled commodities. Oversee that each ration is complete and organized in an orderly stack at the distribution point. Identify vulnerable beneficiaries (widows, pregnant women, the elderly) and ensure they receive priority in collecting their rations. Review, prepare, and submit daily reports of delivered and distributed food. Ensure that all processes are duly recorded and publicly announced to all households within the camp. Ensure that all equipment, food, and supplies are available at the FDP warehouse for the assigned period and daily operations. Mobilize local authorities and the population and raise their awareness about the organization, program objectives, and activities, acting as a link between the organization and beneficiaries at the program site. Validate and verify beneficiaries' information before saving it to the system. Verify beneficiaries' identity during food distributions. Communicate and conduct pre-distribution meetings and disseminate assistance-related information through community-based structures and other mechanisms, including the type and quantity of assistance, the time and date of distribution, and any delays in supplies. Support the integration of accountability practices into program activities by following established procedures during planning, implementation, monitoring, and reporting. Help ensure that accountability is reflected in day-to-day tasks, team interactions, and when working with partners or communities. Support safeguarding of program participants and employees through promoting an environment of awareness and upholding the code of conduct provisions of Medical Teams Protection from Sexual Exploitation & Abuse, Child & Vulnerable Adult protection, and harassment-free workplace policies. Incumbents will remain alert and responsive to any child and adult safeguarding risks, acquire relevant knowledge and skills which will enable you to promote strong safeguarding practices, understand the child and adult safeguarding policy and procedures, and conduct yourself in a manner consistent with the Safeguarding code of conduct and behavior expectations.",
